## Docker inside the container

The container uses the host's docker daemon through its socket (docker-outside-of-docker), which gives it
root-equivalent access to the host. The
[docker-outside-of-docker](https://github.com/devcontainers/features/tree/main/src/docker-outside-of-docker) dev
container feature installs the docker CLI and gives the container user access to the socket.

Containers started from inside run next to the dev container on the host, so paths in `docker run -v` and compose
bind mounts refer to host paths, not container paths. Relative paths resolve to `/home/user/workspace`, which doesn't
exist on the host. Build them from `$LOCAL_WORKSPACE_FOLDER`, the workspace's path on the host, instead:

```yaml
volumes:
  - ${LOCAL_WORKSPACE_FOLDER}/config/params.yaml:/config/params.yaml
```
{%- endif %}

## Git over SSH

VS Code forwards your host's SSH agent into the container, so git over SSH works without mounting `~/.ssh`. Load your
key into the agent on the host first (`ssh-add -l` lists the loaded keys).
